{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>If you do well</b> your deeds, <b>lifted</b> — that is, I will lift my countenance toward you, from the language of (Numbers 6:26) ״ישא ה' פניו אליך״. And He said this to him in response to ויפלו פניו — 'and his face fell.'" "<b>And if you do not do well</b> your deeds, at the opening of the grave (קבורה) shall sin (חטא) be found, crouching (רובץ) — that is, immediately upon your departure from this world you will be punished in the world of souls. Or the phrase לפתח חטאת רובץ may be an allusion to the punishment of חבוט הקבר (the beating of the grave). 'And to you is its desire' — that of the evil inclination (יצה\"ר). 'And you shall rule over it' — if you wish, with the good inclination. And this is what the Midrash (קהלת ט) says: ״ומלט הוא את העיר בחכמתו״. And this is what it says there (Ecclesiastes 9): ״עיר קטנה ואנשים בה מעט ובא אליה מלך גדול וסבב אותה ובנה עליה מצודים גדולים״, ״ומצא בה איש מסכן חכם ומלט הוא את העיר בחכמתו״. It called the body of man 'a small city,' for so it is called 'a small world' (עולם קטן). 'And few people in it' — they are the body's desire and the craving soul, and it called them 'few' because the cravings are many but their attainment is little. 'A great king' — this is the evil inclination, which has many helpers, namely the forces of craving, like a king whose troops are many. 'And surrounded it' — because he encompasses the body from within and from without with evil thoughts and evil deeds, and these are the great siege-works (מצודים) by which man is tripped up. 'A poor wise man' — this is the good inclination, and it is the intellect, and it called him 'poor' (מסכן) because his helpers are few and everything is against him and all hate him, in the manner of what is written (Proverbs 19): ״כל אחי רש שנאוהו״. This is what it says (Ecclesiastes 9): ״ואדם לא זכר את האיש המסכן ההוא״. And it also says there (ibid.): ״וחכמת מסכן בזויה ודבריו אינם נשמעים״. 'And he delivered the city by his wisdom' — this is the good inclination, and it is the intellect: for even though the evil inclination is a great king with many helpers, since the essence of his deeds is only to make the false true and the true false, his downfall is near at the hand of the poor wise man, because a little truth defeats much falsehood, just as a little light defeats much darkness. This is: ״ומלט הוא את העיר בחכמתו״." "<b>It appears</b> to me that Cain sinned in three ways. The first: that he did not believe in HaShem, when He made clear to him in a prophetic vision the truth of punishment and reward. And this is what it says:"], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {1 "Where the Hebrew reads לפתח הקבורה שלך ('at the opening of your grave'), the biblical text reads לפתח חטאת רובץ; the translation preserves R. Bahya's reading with the gloss קבורה and the biblical lemma חטא embedded."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:10:23.406770038Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}